    <item>
      <title>Posts/Blog page</title>
      <link>https://prisma.groningen/help/posts/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://prisma.groningen/help/posts/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The posts address (&amp;lsquo;Blog&amp;rsquo; in the header) is where general publications regarding the group, projects, scientific output, and other announcements should be created. There is no hard set of rules for how these should be formatted, but consider using tags in the header for classification:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific output should have the &amp;lsquo;publication&amp;rsquo; tag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;News, announcements, or similar should have the &amp;rsquo;news&amp;rsquo; tag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re publishing something similar to something else, check if it&amp;rsquo;s tagged in the .md frontmatter, and tag it similarly. The specific tag is less important than consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can always check the existing tags by going to the /tags/ page.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Projects page</title>
      <link>https://prisma.groningen/help/projects/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://prisma.groningen/help/projects/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Projects is where we keep any general information about ongoing PRISMA topics. These should have a general description (preferably public-accessible) for what we&amp;rsquo;re doing. Make sure to include any researchers involved as authors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may wish to link your repository and publications to your project. Use the article shortcode to add any relevant posts in the blog to your project (/posts/your_publication/). Preferably, do not host publications under the projects page. If there is something very relevant to your project that should be permanently linked to it, such as documentations, then it can be added under the /projects/ address.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Camera model identification based on forensic traces extracted from homogeneous patches</title>
      <link>https://prisma.groningen/posts/swaroop_2022_camera/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 01 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://prisma.groningen/posts/swaroop_2022_camera/</guid>
      <description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Highlights 
    &lt;div id=&#34;highlights&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#highlights&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We propose a camera model identification using ConvNets based on homogeneous patches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It consists of a hierarchical (brand, model, and device) classification scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural images contain sufficient homogeneous regions for forensic trace extraction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We achieve 99.01% accuracy on the 18 camera models of the Dresden data set.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With this result, we outperform the state-of-the-art on the same data set.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Abstract 
    &lt;div id=&#34;abstract&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#abstract&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A crucial challenge in digital image forensics is to identify the source camera model used to generate given images. This is of prime importance, especially for Law Enforcement Agencies in their investigations of Child Sexual Abuse Material found in darknets or seized storage devices.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://prisma.groningen/posts/swaroop_2022_camera/featured2022.jpg" />
    </item>
    
  </channel>
</rss>
